OL,3,GNEWSAD-Day veteran receives medals 82
OL,4,Ayears on
OL,5,
OL,6,FA D-Day veteran has received his
OL,7,Fwartime medals more than 80 years after
OL,8,Fthe Normany landings he took part in.
OL,10,FDouglas Halley, from Sheffield, spent
OL,11,Faround eight years serving as a soldier
OL,12,Fin the Royal Artillery, and was present
OL,13,Ffor the invasion in June 1944.
OL,15,FNow, decades after leaving the Army and
OL,16,Fas he rapidly approaches his 103rd
OL,17,Fbirthday, Douglas has received new
OL,18,Fmedals to replace ones he believes he
OL,19,Flost when he was discharged.
OL,21,FLuke Halley, Douglas's grandson, said:
OL,22,F"I was just unbelievably proud."
